content:
The syntax error in the given implementation is the incorrect use of the streaming operator. In SystemVerilog, the streaming operator for bit reversal is `{ << {in} }`, but the syntax `{<<7:0>>{in}}` is not valid. Furthermore, the compiler used in this environment does not support the streaming operator.

To fix this in standard Verilog, you can manually concatenate the bits in reverse order using the concatenation operator `{}`.

```verilog
module top_module (
	input [7:0] in,
	output [7:0] out
);

  assign out = {in[0], in[1], in[2], in[3], in[4], in[5], in[6], in[7]};

endmodule
```
